## On the job {.unnumbered}

::: callout-important
## Why this matters day to day

"How much does department/level/location actually explain?" comes up
constantly — in comp reviews, in engagement analysis, in attrition
discussions. A variance-components model gives you a defensible,
quantified answer instead of an eyeballed one, and the ICC is a genuinely
good one-number summary to put in front of a compensation committee:
it says plainly how much structure there is to explain, before anyone
starts debating why.
:::

